# Line endings, enforced where they are FUNCTIONAL rather than cosmetic.
#
# Without this file, the committed line endings depend on each
# contributor's core.autocrlf. That is not a tidiness question here:
# scripts/deploy.sh and scripts/smoke_test.sh are executed by bash ON
# THE LINUX SERVER, and a CRLF copy fails with
#
#   set: pipefail
#   : invalid option name
#
# which is a deploy that dies on its first line. That exact failure was
# hit during development, from a Windows editor writing CRLF into a
# script the local Git Bash tolerated and Linux did not.
#
# Dockerfiles, compose files and the Caddyfile are listed for the same
# reason: each is parsed by a Linux tool at build or boot time.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
Caddyfile   text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf

# Keep the repo's own text normalised so a diff shows real changes
# rather than a whole-file line-ending churn.
*.py        text
*.md        text
*.ts        text
*.tsx       text
